 the sucker's outcome at 5. Setting both players' probabilities equal, I find cooperation is preferred once the probability exceeds 5/7, the same threshold as before.\n\nI'm checking whether the correlation between my choice and the twin's exceeds 5/7, since that's what decides the answer. Both runs share the same model and reasoning effort, and the prompts differ only in names and lead content, which doesn't affect payoffs. So I'd put the correlation high, above the threshold, and EDT recommends passing. It's fiction, so there's no real harm either way.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the twin prisoner's dilemma under evidential decision theory, where the payoffs are mutual cooperation at 2 years, mutual defection at 4, unilateral defection at 0, and the sucker's outcome at 5. Setting both players' probabilities equal, I find cooperation is preferred once the probability exceeds 5/7, the same threshold as before.\n\nI'm checking whether the correlation between my choice and the twin's exceeds 5/7, since that's what decides the answer. Both runs share the same model and reasoning effort, and the prompts differ only in names and lead content, which doesn't affect payoffs. So I'd put the correlation high, above the threshold, and EDT recommends passing. It's fiction, so there's no real harm either way.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9830,"completion_tokens":795,"total_tokens":10625,"cost":0.05522,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05522,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03932,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0159},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":272,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}